<h2>Structure</h2>
{{{{code}}}}
<html data-theme="light" data-nav="open">
<body>
  <div class="im-shell">
    <header class="im-topbar">…</header>
    <aside  class="im-sidenav">…</aside>
    <main   class="im-shell-main" id="main">…</main>
    <footer class="im-footer">…</footer>
  </div>
  <dialog class="im-navpanel" id="drawer">…</dialog>
</body>
{{{{/code}}}}
<p><code>.im-shell</code> is a CSS grid with named areas. <code>.im-shell-main</code> is a flex column whose children are spaced by <code>--im-section-gap</code>, so a page is just a stack of blocks.</p>

<h2>Three widths of side nav</h2>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-fit" style="--im-grid-min: 11rem">
	<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .5rem"><div class="mini-shell"><span>topbar</span><span>nav</span><span>main</span></div><p class="text-sm text-muted">Open — from <code>lg</code>, by default</p></div>
	<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .5rem"><div class="mini-shell" style="--mini-nav: 2rem"><span>topbar</span><span></span><span>main</span></div><p class="text-sm text-muted">Rail — <code>md</code>…<code>lg</code>, or collapsed</p></div>
	<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .5rem"><div class="mini-shell" style="--mini-nav: 0rem"><span>topbar</span><span></span><span>main</span></div><p class="text-sm text-muted">Drawer — below <code>md</code></p></div>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p>The rail hides labels with CSS only; they stay in the DOM for screen readers, and each link's <code>title</code> gives the tooltip. The visitor's choice is <code>&lt;html data-nav="rail"&gt;</code>, stored, and applied before first paint by <code>partials/shell/head-script.hbs</code>.</p>

<h2>Top bar</h2>
<p>Three columns: start (nav toggle, brand), a centred search button, end (actions). The search "field" is a button that opens a dialog — in Ghost, leave <code>data-ghost-search</code> on it and Ghost's own search opens.</p>
{{#example flush=true}}
<div style="--im-gutter: 1rem; position: relative">
	<header class="im-topbar" style="position: static">
		<div class="im-topbar-start"><button class="im-btn im-btn-ghost im-btn-icon" type="button" aria-label="Collapse">{{> "icons/panel-left"}}</button><a class="im-brand" href="#top-bar">Publication</a></div>
		<div class="im-topbar-search"><button class="im-searchbar" type="button">{{> "icons/search"}}<span>Search</span><kbd>/</kbd></button></div>
		<div class="im-topbar-end"><a class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-btn-primary" href="#top-bar">Subscribe</a></div>
	</header>
</div>
{{/example}}
{{{{code}}}}
{{#> "shell/topbar"}}
  <span class="im-badge">Beta</span>        ← optional: anything after the brand
{{/"shell/topbar"}}
{{{{/code}}}}

<h2>Side nav</h2>
<p>One class, <code>.im-navlink</code>, inside <code>.im-navgroup</code>s. The current page is <code>aria-current="page"</code> — no "active" class to keep in step.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 16rem"}}
<div class="im-navgroup">
	<p class="im-navgroup-title">Writing</p>
	<a class="im-navlink" href="#side-nav" aria-current="page">{{> "icons/house"}}<span>Home</span></a>
	<a class="im-navlink" href="#side-nav">{{> "icons/book-open"}}<span>Journal</span></a>
	<a class="im-navlink" href="#side-nav">{{> "icons/video"}}<span>Videos</span></a>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Article with a rail</h2>
<p><code>.im-with-aside</code> is a reading column plus a sticky rail — this page. Below <code>lg</code> the rail moves above the article. Put <code>&lt;nav class="im-toc" data-toc="#article"&gt;</code> in it and <code>im.js</code> builds the table of contents from the article's <code>h2</code> and <code>h3</code>.</p>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-with-aside</code></td><td>Reading column, then a 13.5rem rail. Its width <strong>follows the side nav</strong>: collapse the nav and the space it gives up goes to the content.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-with-aside-wide</code></td><td>A 19rem column — wide enough for real <a href="/components/widgets/">widgets</a> rather than a contents rail.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-with-aside-start</code></td><td>The column on the left. Only the tracks swap; nothing moves in the markup.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Below <code>lg</code> both fold to one column. A <strong>contents</strong> rail moves above the article, because it is a way in; a <strong>wide</strong> column stays below it, because it is further reading. <a href="/collections/post/single/">A full article</a> has all three on a switch.</p>

