<h2>Not every page has a sidebar</h2>
<p>Three shells, one system. The <strong>docs shell</strong> (top bar + side nav) is this site. A <strong>top-bar-only</strong> site drops the side nav and keeps <code>im-topbar</code>; the content layouts do not notice. A <strong>single page</strong> — a post, a lesson, a trip — decides its own right rail with <code>data-sidebar="on|off"</code> on <code>im-single</code>, and a collection page can carry a rail or run full width (<a href="/collections/wishlist/">the bucket list</a>, <a href="/collections/travel/">travel</a>). The <a href="/collections/snippets/page/">snippet page</a> uses a left rail instead. None of these are separate layouts — they are the same grid with a column switched off.</p>
